fect crew.\n\nGiven the evidence, perhaps Candidate C's ability to anticipate dangerous situations and see complex connections is highly valuable for long-distance flights, outweighing unfriendly attitude? But crew cooperation is essential; unfriendly could be a problem.\n\nWe could argue that we need to discuss B, C, D before final decision, but we can give provisional recommendation still A, but note that B's stress handling is a strong point that could challenge A. Or we could shift to B.\n\nGiven the instruction to cover all candidates before final, we should bring up a new candidate and compare. Perhaps we can say: I see strong stress resilience in B, which is critical, and his technical competence is solid, but his communication style is concerning. Compared to A's communication difficulty, B's issues may be more manageable. Therefore I am less convinced that A is the best; I think B might be a stronger overall fit.\n\nThus we can change vote to Candidate B, providing evidence: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress very well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical). Concern: pretentious, wrong tone (communication). Explain why this may be less severe than A's egocentric and difficulty communicating ideas.\n\nLet's do that: change vote to Candidate B.\n\nWe must reference Agent 1's point. Provide evidence from our notes. Provide implication.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B."}
